shape theory.coherence : theory.contact.self {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 5.6 (Coherence).
// A structure S is coherent when it can produce well-defined
// transformation at every moment. This requires three conditions:
//   (1) all contacts through which character enters transformation
//       are stable
//   (2) transformation conserves structure
//   (3) coupled incompatible shapes resolve
//
// Laws 1-3 derive why each condition is necessary.
// Theorem 5.9 proves they are jointly sufficient.
//
// Derives from: theory.contact.self
//               (coherence is derivable from self-contact alone)
  """
}
